# rdtroubleshoot — optional credentials
#
#   cp .env_template .env
#   chmod 600 .env
#
# Everything here is OPTIONAL. With no .env the tool still runs every check it can answer
# as an ordinary user; the privileged ones report what they could not inspect and why, and
# the exit code does not move.
#
# .env is gitignored. Never commit it.
#
# Two things the tool does with what you put here, so you can judge the risk:
#   - A secret is never printed, never logged, and never placed on a command line. A sudo
#     password goes down the child process's stdin (`sudo -S`) and nowhere else, because
#     argv is world-readable through /proc.
#   - If this file is group- or world-readable, the tool reports that as a FAILURE and
#     REFUSES to use the secrets in it. Using them would tell you everything is fine while
#     your root password sits in a file anyone on the box can read. So: chmod 600.


# --- privileged local checks -------------------------------------------------------
# The sudo password for THIS machine. Unlocks the checks that cannot be answered as an
# ordinary user:
#   - the full SELinux audit log (`ausearch -m avc`), which lives in /var/log/audit and
#     is root-only. Without it the tool reads the journal instead, which carries most AVC
#     records but not all of them.
#   - system Flatpak overrides under /var/lib/flatpak/overrides, which is where a
#     system-scope permission change is recorded.
#   - `rpm-ostree status` details on some configurations.
#
# Leave it empty if you would rather run the two or three commands by hand; the tool
# prints them in its `fix` lines.
RDT_SUDO_PASSWORD=

# --- remote troubleshooting ---------------------------------------------------------
# The RetroDECK machine, when you are diagnosing it from somewhere else. Used only in the
# command suggestions the tool prints; it never opens an SSH connection by itself.
# Format: user@host, or a Host alias from ~/.ssh/config.
RDT_SSH_TARGET=retro@retrodeck-box

# --- RetroDECK locations ------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed when RetroDECK is not in the default place. A real environment variable
# still wins over these, so a one-off `RETRODECK_ROMS=... ./rdtroubleshoot` works.
# Defaults: ~/retrodeck, then $RDT_RETRODECK_HOME/roms and /ES-DE.
RDT_RETRODECK_HOME=~/retrodeck
#RDT_ROMS=~/retrodeck/roms
#RDT_ESDE=~/retrodeck/ES-DE

# --- ScreenScraper -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Only used to cross-check what is already in ~/.skyscraper/config.ini — the tool does no
# scraping and makes no network request. Point of the check: a half-set credential
# (`userCreds="user:"`) sends an empty password on every request, so login is refused and
# a long unattended run scrapes nothing while exiting 0.
#
# Note that Skyscraper does NOT URL-encode this password: characters like " $ ; > & are
# hazardous there, and ';' can act as a query separator server-side. Use an alphanumeric
# one.
SS_USER=exampleuser
SS_PASS=
